      "category": "network_architecture",
      "rationale": "Reduce the GRU state width to 75% and learn a linear adapter back to the unchanged embedding dimension before history aggregation. This may reduce recurrent compute and overfitting. Preserve embeddings, readout, scoring, loss, optimizer, and dataset routing. The generated predictor imports this same model class, so it reconstructs the adapted architecture when loading each category's single checkpoint.",
      "edits": [
        {
          "find": "        dropout = dropout_rate if num_layers > 1 else 0.0\n        self.gru = nn.GRU(hidden_units, hidden_units, num_layers=num_layers,\n                          batch_first=True, dropout=dropout)\n        self.dropout = nn.Dropout(dropout_rate)",
          "replace": "        dropout = dropout_rate if num_layers > 1 else 0.0\n        self.recurrent_units = max(1, (3 * hidden_units) // 4)\n        self.gru = nn.GRU(hidden_units, self.recurrent_units, num_layers=num_layers,\n                          batch_first=True, dropout=dropout)\n        self.output_adapter = nn.Linear(self.recurrent_units, hidden_units)\n        self.dropout = nn.Dropout(dropout_rate)"
        },
        {
          "find": "    def encode(self, seq: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:\n        emb = self.dropout(self.item_emb(seq))\n        out, _ = self.gru(emb)\n        out = self.aggregate_states(out, seq)",
